{
  "description": "A compatibility adapter that lets Self-EvolveRec diagnose trained recommendation models while preserving the RecHarness benchmark protocol. DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader) returns metrics and metric_definitions.",
  "motivation": "Keep diagnostics compatible with architecture changes, grounded in available public data, and aligned with the shared validation objective.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain the required class and method signatures. Access the actual trained module through view.model and adapt probes to its architecture. Preserve the view interfaces item_emb, log2feats, predict_score, user_train, meta_data, and review_data without fabricating unavailable data. Batches contain (None, sequence, positive, negative), with tensors shaped B x L. Only interaction histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps are available; review content, ratings, item attributes beyond those fields, and simulator diversity/conformity traits are unavailable. Generate full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for twenty real training users, five per category. Preserve all four dataset routes and select models using macro-average validation HR@10 under the pinned evaluator.",
  "pseudocode": "class DiagnosisProbe:\n    initialize(view, device)\n    run_full_diagnosis(train_loader):\n        access trained model through view.model\n        inspect batches using architecture-compatible probes\n        compute only diagnostics supported by observed data\n        record definitions and unavailable diagnostics explicitly\n        return metrics, metric_definitions\n\nFor simulator input:\n    for each of four categories:\n        generate full-catalog unseen-item recommendations\n        for five designated real training users\n\nFor model selection:\n    use the pinned evaluator's macro validation HR@10",
  "originality": {
    "score": 3,
    "positive": "Provides a concrete bridge between native diagnostics and a controlled recommendation benchmark.",
    "negative": "Defines an integration contract rather than a new recommendation algorithm."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Can support architecture changes and comparable, evidence-grounded diagnostic feedback.",
    "negative": "Its value depends on probe quality; unavailable traits cannot be directly diagnosed."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 5,
    "positive": "Explicit interfaces and batch shapes make the adapter straightforward to structure.",
    "negative": "Architecture-specific probes and compatibility views require careful validation."
  }
}
